# Céluma clinical / anatomical-pathology supplementary lexicon (es) — SOURCE asset.
#
# This file is the reviewable source of `clinical-es.dic` (generated by
# `scripts/build_clinical_lexicon.mjs`; never edit the .dic by hand). It is
# loaded in addition to — never instead of — the unmodified upstream RLA-ES
# dictionary (`../dictionaries/es-MX`), and it is written against that
# dictionary's own affix flags so gender and number forms follow the same rules:
#
#   term        invariable form only
#   term/S      plural by the upstream rules (noun, or adjective invariable in gender)
#   term/GS     feminine + plural forms (adjective or noun ending in -o/-e/-án/-ón…)
#   Term/..     a capitalised entry is a proper name: it matches only when capitalised
#
# Sections: `## <id> | <class> | <description>`.
#   class R = word supplied by the owner as correctly written (reviewed example)
#   class T = standard Spanish medical / anatomical-pathology terminology listed by the
#             change author for the owner's clinical reviewers. NOT yet signed off by a
#             clinician: the lexicon is a reviewable proposal, not a validated terminology.
# Suggested verification references for reviewers (none is copied here): Real Academia
# Nacional de Medicina, Diccionario de términos médicos; Diccionario de la lengua española
# (RAE); WHO Classification of Tumours (Spanish usage); ICD-O-3 / CIE-O-3 topography and
# morphology terms. Every entry must stay a lexical item: no abbreviations with digits,
# no patient names, no copied report text.
#
# Entries the upstream dictionary already accepts are harmless: the build step reports
# and omits them.

